{
  "lang": "en",
  "kind": "how",
  "title": "Shell palette — nodes, groups, edges",
  "pattern": "You Don't Know · debug surface",
  "repo": "you-dont-know",
  "thesis": "One locked shell. Stadium, fork, Lucide cloud, groups, trees, node icons, edge kinds — without restyling :root.",
  "problem": "Custom polygon shells (parallelogram, wave, cylinder, hexagon, freehand cloud) alias against the grid and miss ortho arrow ports.",
  "whyNotBasic": "A unique SVG outline per kind breaks ports. Rect and stadium stay; `decision` is a rect with a fork glyph; cloud is Lucide on a stadium, not a blob path.",
  "cost": "No ISO data / document / store / cpu shells. Aliases (`child`→`process`, `hoc`→`frame`) stay valid.",
  "asides": [
    {
      "id": "color-lock",
      "title": "Three hues, three fixed roles",
      "body": "Three roles, fixed: `--color-primary` is focus and structure, `--color-accent` marks the current material, `--color-accent-2` is status. `boundary` is peach in every lesson. `kind` tones one dot and repaints nothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "group-parent",
      "title": "How a group is built",
      "body": "A node with `kind: \"group\"` is a fence. Children set `parent` to that id. The shell sizes the fence around them. The group id still belongs in some `steps[].highlight`."
    }
  ],
  "files": ["references/lesson-contract.md"],
