    {
      "id": "runtime",
      "title": "Architecture glyphs",
      "narration": "Lucide 24×24, `currentColor`, stroke 2. `boundary` keeps `--color-accent-2`. `child` / `other` / `hoc` still alias.",
      "highlight": ["g-run", "provider", "host", "frame", "inbox", "action", "boundary", "junction", "subroutine"],
      "code": {
        "file": "templates/lesson.html",
        "startLine": 1,
        "text": "kindOf({ kind: \"hoc\" }) // → \"frame\"\nkindOf({ kind: \"child\" }) // → \"process\""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fence",
      "title": "Group fence",
      "narration": "Dashed frame with its own fill. Children set `parent`. [[group-parent]].",
      "highlight": ["g-iso", "g-run", "g-tree"],
      "code": {
        "file": "lesson.json",
        "startLine": 1,
        "text": "{ \"id\": \"g-iso\", \"label\": \"ISO flowchart\", \"kind\": \"group\" }\n{ \"id\": \"cloud\", \"kind\": \"cloud\", \"parent\": \"g-iso\" }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tree",
      "title": "Folder list",
      "narration": "Folder / file glyphs in a one-column fence. A lesson that is only folders uses `layout: \"tree\"` for indent.",
      "highlight": ["g-tree", "dir-src", "dir-pages", "file-main", "file-types"],
      "code": {
        "file": "lesson.json",
        "startLine": 1,
        "text": "{ \"layout\": \"tree\" }\n{ \"id\": \"src\", \"kind\": \"folder\", \"label\": \"src/\" }\n{ \"id\": \"app\", \"kind\": \"file\", \"label\": \"app.ts\", \"parent\": \"src\" }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edges",
      "title": "Edge kinds",
      "narration": "`flow` default. `dashed` async. `back` reverse marker. `both` two heads. `via` bends through a junction.",
      "highlight": ["start", "process", "decision", "cloud", "queue", "action", "junction", "inbox", "host", "boundary", "provider", "frame", "subroutine"],
      "code": {
        "file": "lesson.json",
        "startLine": 1,
        "text": "{ \"from\": \"cloud\", \"to\": \"queue\", \"kind\": \"back\", \"label\": \"retry\" }\n{ \"from\": \"action\", \"to\": \"inbox\", \"via\": \"junction\" }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lines",
      "title": "Line types and tones",
      "narration": "`line`: solid · dashed · dotted · chain. `tone`: ink-soft · ink · primary · accent-2 — a token, never coral. Nothing is lit here; on the previous step the same three edges are, and turn coral whatever their tone while keeping their line.",
      "highlight": ["g-run", "provider", "frame"],
      "code": {
        "file": "lesson.json",
        "startLine": 1,
        "text": "{ \"from\": \"provider\", \"to\": \"host\", \"line\": \"dotted\", \"tone\": \"primary\" }\n{ \"from\": \"frame\", \"to\": \"subroutine\", \"line\": \"chain\", \"tone\": \"ink\" }\n{ \"from\": \"host\", \"to\": \"boundary\", \"tone\": \"accent-2\" }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "icons",
      "title": "Node icons",
      "narration": "`kind` sets the shape and the role in the flow; `icon` says what the thing is. The names are generic — data, code, network, time — so any lesson can use them, and a process box with `\"icon\": \"database\"` is still a process box.",
      "highlight": ["g-icons", "icon-user", "icon-browser", "icon-screen", "icon-component", "icon-terminal", "icon-function", "icon-package", "icon-link", "icon-config", "icon-state", "icon-rules", "icon-database", "icon-cache", "icon-disk", "icon-lock", "icon-key", "icon-route", "icon-server", "icon-request", "icon-response", "icon-broadcast", "icon-mail", "icon-retry", "icon-timer", "icon-limit", "icon-trace", "icon-error", "icon-mock"],
